    ],
    "source_pages": [
      4
    ],
    "text": "Our model\u2019s output consists of two maps: one with the probability distribution of the criminal\u2019s location and one with the prediction of the location of his/her next crime. The probabilities are displayed in bands of color: a red band represents an area of high priority and a blue band represents one of low priority. In the case of attempting to locate the criminal, we suggest searching the red areas \ufb01rst. In the case of trying to prevent a future crime, we suggest spreading as many o\ufb03cers as possible in the red and yellow bands, as these regions are likely to contain the criminal\u2019s next target."
  },
